    "UiNewTabCreatedParams": {
      "description": "Client notification `ui/newTab/created` (UI → core): the pane created the tab that request `openRequestId` (a `ui/openRequested` visualize open with `openUrl`) asked for, and this is the page's agent-facing id (`p…`), Node's `watchNewTab(...).page`.\n\nSemantics, from `main/browser/new-tab-waiters.ts`: the core starts waiting when it publishes the open and answers the agent's `open` with this page id. Only a report whose `sessionId` and `openRequestId` both match the pending open settles it, once; a tab nobody named (the user's \"+\"), another request's tab or a different session's says nothing about it. There is no negative report: a pane that drops or replaces the request sends nothing, so the wait ends with no page id after 3000 ms, or when the open is cancelled, a new open reuses the request id, or the session's browser is released. With no page id the agent is told to find the page with the browser tool's `list_tabs`.",
      "properties": {
        "openRequestId": {
          "type": "string"
        },
        "pageId": {
          "type": "string"
        },
        "sessionId": {
          "type": "string"
        }
      },
      "required": [
        "openRequestId",
        "pageId",
        "sessionId"
      ],
      "type": "object"
    },
    "UiScreenSessionsChangedParams": {
      "description": "Client notification `ui/screenSessions/changed` (UI → core): the sessions the user is looking at right now. Node asks `isSessionOnScreen(sessionId)` (`screen-sessions.ts`) at each delivery: true only while the window is visible, not minimized and focused, and its page reports painting that session. The host applies those window conditions itself, so this is the effective set: empty while the window is hidden, minimized or unfocused, or its page is gone (reload, navigation, renderer crash). It is a full replacement, sent on every change of the set (a report from the page, focus, blur, minimize, hide, show) and once when the UI attaches. The core treats a session as on screen only while it is in the latest set, and treats a detached UI as an empty set. No response.\n\nA paired phone sends the same notification over its relay connection, with its page visibility and app foreground applied. `browserId` is the id its direct Web Push subscription is keyed by (Node's `setForeground(visible, browserId)`): at most 64 UTF-16 units, kept until the phone states another, and ignored on every connection that is not a relay connection.\n\nOn a relay connection two more optional fields carry what Node's phone sent as `setForeground` and `setVisualizePanels`: `foreground` (false = the app is backgrounded; a connection starts in the foreground) and `visualizeSessionIds` (the sessions whose visualize panel the page shows; none until stated). Each is kept until the phone states another, and ignored on every connection that is not a relay connection. A paired phone counts as viewing a session's visualize panel (`hostState` key `remoteViewing`) only while attached, in the foreground and with that session in `visualizeSessionIds` (Node's `clientViewsSessionLane`).",
      "properties": {
        "browserId": {
          "type": [
            "string",
            "null"
          ]
        },
        "foreground": {
          "type": [
            "boolean",
            "null"
          ]
        },
        "sessionIds": {
          "description": "Absent only from a paired phone stating one of the other fields alone (Node's `setForeground` or `setVisualizePanels`): its last set stays. A UI's notification without it changes nothing.",
          "items": {
            "type": "string"
          },
          "type": [
            "array",
            "null"
          ]
        },
        "visualizeSessionIds": {
          "items": {
            "type": "string"
          },
          "type": [
            "array",
            "null"
          ]
        }
      },
      "type": "object"
    },
    "UiTerminalRunClaimedParams": {
      "description": "Client notification `ui/terminalRun/claimed` (UI → core): a pane now shows the terminal of a `ui/openRequested` terminal open that carried `requestId`.\n\nNo response. The core waits for the claim 2000 ms (the renderer's 1500 ms shown-wait plus 500 ms for the claim's trip back) and then settles the run as `shown: false`, reported to the agent as running in the background; with no UI attached it settles `shown: false` at once. A claim settles its run once: a claim for an unknown or already-settled id has no effect.",
      "properties": {
        "requestId": {
          "type": "string"
        }
      },
      "required": [
        "requestId"
      ],
      "type": "object"
    }
  },
